From: Eric Tanner <eric.tanner@harvia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: vt-sbc-am62l: bring the panel backlight up at 100/255, not full

The pwm-backlight node asked for default-brightness-level 255, so the
kernel lit the panel at full duty the moment it probed - before any
userspace policy could run. Full scale on this panel is brighter than the
product wants and draws more backlight current than it needs.

Start at 100. The rootfs (set-display-rotation.sh, then the SignaSteam app)
writes the same level, so the panel comes up once at the product level and
stays there.

This does not cap max_brightness: pwm-backlight always maps the largest
brightness-levels entry to 100% duty, so shrinking the table would only
relabel the scale, not limit the current. The cap is enforced by every
writer in the rootfs using 100.

Signed-off-by: Eric Tanner <eric.tanner@harvia.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/vt-sbc-am62l.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/vt-sbc-am62l.dtsi
@@ -195,7 +195,7 @@
 			240 241 242 243 244 245 246 247
 			248 249 250 251 252 253 254 255
 		>;
-		default-brightness-level = <255>;
+		default-brightness-level = <100>;
 	};
 	watchdog_gpio: watchdog-gpio {
 		compatible ="linux,wdt-gpio";
